{
  "_doc": "Main Street's dressing in the valley (#1304, art's; ValleyStreetDressing: src/art/valley_street_dressing.gd). What each owner puts out before his lot (`lots`, by valley.json's lot id) and what stands in the street itself (`street`). A lot's things stand `along` m east from its x0 and `out` m off its front (minus is into the street: the walk is 0 to -2.4, its street edge -2.4, the street's middle -10.05); the street's at `x` and `z` (north is minus). Each stands on what's there (a walk's planks or the ground) plus `up`. Kinds: `kit` (a prop kit id; `n` of them `step` [along, out] apart, `rows` stacked `layer` m apart, every one of a row turned `turn` degrees more), `rail` (a HitchingRail `rail` m long along the street, `horses` tied to it a stall apart, nose to the rail, on its street side), `trough` (a WaterTrough `trough` m long), `wagon` (a kit wagon; its tongue toward -X turned by `yaw`; `team` horses standing in its traces), `horse` (standing loose, head toward -X turned by `yaw`). Entries with the same `pile` on a lot are one heap and may touch; any others stand at least `GAP_M` (0.9 m) apart, so there's no slot a man walks into and sticks. Never on a way: a thing within `clear_m` of a town link (ValleyTown.add_ways: the doors' flights, the passages' mouths, the street's spine) or of a folk's spot and its way to the places nearest it (valley_folk.json) is left out and said so (the test: none left out). Not in this file: the livery's rail, which is RideThere's (config/ride_there.json's `town`).",
